      "purpose": "Provides reusable TypeScript control-flow utilities for typed result construction, exhaustive switch validation, assertions, externally controlled promises, and delays.",
      "summary": "This module centralizes small control primitives used across the package. It defines a discriminated success-or-error result representation with factory helpers, runtime assertions that improve TypeScript narrowing, an exhaustive-switch error utility, a deferred promise abstraction, and a timer-based sleep helper. Error-producing assertions delegate stack-trace cleanup to an imported wrapper.",
      "businessContext": "Supports reliable application control flow and typed error handling across utility consumers. Failures can cause incorrect result propagation, weak runtime validation, or broken async coordination.",
